I left out the `http-client` import and the enrichment call. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`, and the graph definition hasn't been updated to add `http-client`. Sending each customer's question in a query string to an outside host would also send customer content off-platform, so I didn't implement that part. The crate below uses only the granted inference interface. Once the graph grants `http-client` and the enrichment's destination and data handling are specified, that change can be made as a separate step.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{customer-query, moderation-result};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: customer-query) -> moderation-result;
}
